# Everything under .local/share/nvim is generated state, not configuration:
# mason's installed language servers, treesitter queries, telescope history,
# netrw history. mason and packer write ABSOLUTE symlinks into it
# (/home/piero/.local/share/nvim/mason/packages/...), and stow refuses an
# absolute symlink outright -- "source is an absolute symlink ... All
# operations aborted" -- which aborts the whole stow invocation.
#
# None of it is worth carrying between machines, and none of it is in git:
# .gitignore already excludes it, so a fresh clone never has it. This file
# matters on a machine whose working tree does (this desktop, re-running
# bootstrap). packer clones itself on first launch -- nvim-config's
# plugins.lua -- and installs the rest. Wallpapers, the other half of this
# package, still stow.
^/\.local/share/nvim$
